# sshd configuration for `kobe ssh-proxy`.
#
# `kobe-sshd` runs this as the workload user in inetd mode (`sshd -i`): one
# session per process, served over the attach stream's stdin and stdout.
# Nothing listens on a port, so `exposedPorts` is not involved and the pool
# needs no Service. The host key path is supplied by `kobe-sshd` because it
# lives under $HOME, which the image does not fix at build time.
#
# Only the workload user can log in: sshd running without root cannot switch
# identity, and `AllowUsers` makes the intent explicit rather than implied.
AllowUsers nonroot
AuthorizedKeysFile %h/.ssh/authorized_keys
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitRootLogin no
UsePAM no
StrictModes yes
PermitUserEnvironment no
AcceptEnv LANG LC_* COLORTERM
PidFile none
LogLevel ERROR
Subsystem sftp /usr/lib/openssh/sftp-server
